From edc793362851327be55285beb1ef78039c870da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:58:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: Level 1 performance.timing with epoch times;
 timeOrigin on the Unix epoch

performance.timing returned the Level 2 PerformanceNavigationTiming entry,
which has no navigationStart, so loadEventEnd - navigationStart was NaN.
LinkedIn aborts its startup on that and never loads its icons. It is now
the Level 1 PerformanceTiming interface with milliseconds since the Unix
epoch. timeOrigin was offset from the platform's monotonic epoch (boot
time on Linux) rather than the Unix epoch; both now convert through the
wall clock. fetchStart, the DNS/connect attributes, requestStart,
responseStart and domLoading are filled in, so performance.measure()
accepts them instead of throwing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
